        scene: 'You are on a Lean assignment at a builder of packaging machines. The 70-person software department is moving to SAFe. The operations director asks you in the corridor: “You understand this agile stuff. What is this train, and what will I notice of it in the factory?”',
        ask: 'Explain it in two minutes, in his language.',
        model: '“The train is the group of about seven software teams that together make the controls for our machines. They plan together every ten weeks, in two days, and after that they deliver something that works every two weeks. For you it means: one fixed moment where you hear what is coming in the next ten weeks, and a place to put your priorities. Just like takt on the line: a fixed rhythm, so everyone can count on each other.”',
